---
title: "What happens when I enter dhwanijain.me and press Enter (Railway, with Azure changes)"
---
flowchart LR
  ASSUME["<b>Assumptions</b><br/>no cached DNS answer<br/>typed dhwanijain.me → browser tries http,<br/>gets 301 to https, follows it<br/><br/><b>① Browser parses the URL</b><br/>scheme http · host dhwanijain.me<br/>port 80 · path /"]

  subgraph HOME["MY SIDE · at home AP + switch + router are one box, on campus they are separate"]
    direction TB
    LAP["<b>Laptop</b><br/>browser · OS resolver · Wi-Fi card<br/>DHCP gave: private IP, subnet mask,<br/>default gateway, DNS server"]
    AP["<b>Access point</b>"]
    SW["<b>Switch</b><br/>connects devices on the LAN"]
    RT["<b>Router</b> = default gateway<br/>NAT: private source IP → public IP,<br/>maps the reply back<br/>stateful firewall lets the reply in"]
    MOD["<b>Modem / ONT</b>"]
    LAP ---|Wi-Fi| AP
    AP --- SW
    SW --- RT
    RT --- MOD
  end

  subgraph NET["INTERNET"]
    direction TB
    ISP["<b>ISP</b><br/>name: unknown"]
    IR["<b>Internet routers</b><br/>forward hop by hop by IP"]
    ISP --- IR
  end

  subgraph DNSG["② DNS · a separate exchange, finished before the web request"]
    direction TB
    RES["<b>Recursive resolver</b><br/>location: check with scutil --dns"]
    ROOT["Root servers"]
    TLD[".me servers"]
    CF["<b>Cloudflare</b>, authoritative<br/>@ CNAME 8udvcs1q.up.railway.app<br/>flattened → Railway edge A records"]
    RES -.->|"referral"| ROOT
    RES -.->|"referral"| TLD
    RES -.->|"answer"| CF
  end

  subgraph RW["RAILWAY (host I draw fully)"]
    direction TB
    EDGE["<b>Railway edge</b><br/>public IP · :80 and :443<br/>holds the certificate<br/><b>TLS ENDS HERE</b>"]
    APP["<b>Container</b><br/>Uvicorn, 2 workers, on $PORT<br/>FastAPI home → load_profile → Jinja"]
    PG[("<b>PostgreSQL</b> :5432<br/>Railway private network")]
    EDGE -->|"⑦ plain HTTP on $PORT · private<br/>X-Forwarded-Proto: https<br/>C: edge · S: Uvicorn"| APP
    APP -->|"⑧ SQL over TCP 5432<br/>private DATABASE_URL<br/>C: app · S: Postgres"| PG
  end

  GOOG["<b>Google</b><br/>googletagmanager.com · google-analytics.com"]

  subgraph AZ["WHAT CHANGES ON AZURE"]
    direction TB
    AZDNS["DNS answer: @ A 4.155.216.147<br/>(not a flattened CNAME)"]
    NSG["<b>NSG</b> firewall<br/>80, 443 from any · 22 only from my laptop /32<br/>8000: no rule"]
    PIP["Public IP 4.155.216.147 (Azure holds it)<br/>→ VM private IP 172.16.0.4"]
    NGX["<b>Nginx</b> :443 · Certbot / Let's Encrypt cert<br/><b>TLS ENDS HERE</b>"]
    UV["<b>Uvicorn</b> 127.0.0.1:8000<br/>2 workers · systemd"]
    DB[("<b>SQLite file</b><br/>data/resume.db")]
    AZDNS ~~~ NSG
    NSG --> PIP --> NGX
    NGX -->|"plain HTTP over loopback"| UV
    UV -->|"file read, no network"| DB
  end

  ASSUME ~~~ LAP
  MOD --- ISP
  LAP -.->|"② DNS query, UDP 53<br/>C: laptop · S: resolver<br/>(crosses the same hardware)"| RES
  IR ==>|"③ HTTP :80 → 301 to https<br/>④ TCP handshake to :443<br/>⑤ TLS: SNI, cert name/dates/chain → keys<br/>⑥ GET / · Host: dhwanijain.me (encrypted)<br/>C: laptop · S: Railway edge"| EDGE
  EDGE ==>|"⑨ 200 + HTML, re-encrypted<br/>same path back · router un-NATs it"| IR
  LAP -->|"⑩ further requests: CSS from the edge (same connection)<br/>gtag.js + page_view hit to Google (new DNS, TCP, TLS)"| GOOG
  RW ~~~ AZ

